specflat is a SDSS product built for the BOSS idlspec2D pipeline. 



It contains a number of products:
    pixflatave-{MJD}-{b/r}{1/2}.fits
        - average pixel-to-pixel flat fields
        - Produced by spflatave.pro (idlspec2d) from pixflat-{MJD}-{b/r}{1/2}.fits produced by spflatgen.pro (idlspec2d)
    badpixels-{MJD}-{b/r}{1/2}.fits
        - a bad pixel mask (including hot pixels) from from a set of darks and biases
        - Produced by combinebpm.pro (idlspec2d)
    boss_pixbias-{MJD}-{b/r}{1/2}.fits.gz 
        - 4-amplifier master bias frame 
        - Produced by bolton_biasgen.pro (idlspec2d)
        - replaced the historical pixbiasave product
    pixbiasave-{MJD}-{b/r}{1/2}.fits.gz -  
        - Historical product - 4-amplifier master bias frame
        - Produced by spbiasave.pro (idlspec2d) from pixbias-{MJD}-{b/r}{1/2}.fits produced by spbiasgen.pro (idlspec2d)
   

It also contains the idl procedures to generate lossy-fiber pixflats 
